"*initramfs* – initial ramdisk containing script to setup snapshot devices "
"(see below) and mount /lib/modules"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/system/template-implementation.rst:48
#: 6bdeeed6ea994c689f9f42b1736dfb23
msgid ""
"*modules.img* – filesystem image of /lib/modules with matching kernel "
"modules and firmware (/lib/firmware/updates is symlinked to /lib/modules/"
"firmware)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/system/template-implementation.rst:52
#: a016c68e602c4974a60435db335d30b3
msgid ""
"Normally kernel “package” is common for many VMs (can be set using qvm-"
"prefs). One of them can be set as default (qvm-set-default-kernel) to "
"simplify kernel updates (by default all VMs use the default kernel). All "
"installed kernels are placed in /var/lib/qubes/vm-kernels as separate "
"subdirs. In this case, modules.img is attached to the VM as R/O device."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/system/template-implementation.rst:54
#: e53e33cee9304620b2f50c9fe40c6671
msgid ""
"There is a special case when the VM can have a custom kernel – when it is "
"updateable (StandaloneVM or TemplateVM) and the kernel is set to “none” (by "
"qvm-prefs). In this case the VM uses the kernel from the “kernels” VM subdir "
"and modules.img is attached as R/W device."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/system/template-implementation.rst:57
#: 7004853769054d1f8bd523279c150626
msgid "Qubes TemplateVM implementation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/system/template-implementation.rst:60
#: 2f5c4895a80143d2a190284508044912
msgid ""
"TemplateVM has a shared root.img across all AppVMs that are based on it. "
"This mechanism has some advantages over a simple common device connected to "
"multiple VMs:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/system/template-implementation.rst:62
#: 3ce6087c932b4b3a83475e802f4c8fdf
msgid ""
"root.img can be modified while there are AppVMs running – without corrupting "
"the filesystem"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/system/template-implementation.rst:64
#: 4bfbfd5d0fa04bf8891bedf496477e17
msgid ""
"multiple AppVMs that are using different versions of root.img (from various "
"points in time) can be running concurrently"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/system/template-implementation.rst:68
#: 00b871fdd8224c6a9d3a3f5f8655c241
msgid ""
"There are two layers of the device-mapper snapshot device; the first one "
"enables modifying root.img without stopping the AppVMs and the second one, "
"which is contained in the AppVM, enables temporal modifications to its "
"filesystem. These modifications will be discarded after a restart of the "
"AppVM."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/system/template-implementation.rst:70
#: 202eca51d56a483a9c94604d7499ae65
msgid "TemplateSharing2.png"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/system/template-implementation.rst:76
#: 250ae8ac6cf942d1971a8cc38418b34a
msgid "Snapshot device in Dom0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/system/template-implementation.rst:79
#: 64f0fc11492748f7ae020578aa6c9b2b
msgid "This device consists of:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/system/template-implementation.rst:81
#: 3e0bd54701cf4f6c9f397b2c3214b14f
msgid "root.img – real template filesystem"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/system/template-implementation.rst:83
#: 9e4dc34cefe749f4902957b96fc9afe2
msgid ""
"root-cow.img – differences between the device as seen by AppVM and the "
"current root.img"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/system/template-implementation.rst:87
#: 1b852112e9964da987ee68edfd0e7fb8
msgid ""
"The above is achieved through creating device-mapper snapshots for each "
"version of root.img. When an AppVM is started, a xen hotplug script (/etc/"
"xen/scripts/block-snapshot) reads the inode numbers of root.img and root-"
"cow.img; these numbers are used as the snapshot device’s name. When a device "
"with the same name exists the new AppVM will use it – therefore, AppVMs "
"based on the same version of root.img will use the same device. Of course, "
"the device-mapper cannot use the files directly – it must be connected "
"through /dev/loop*. The same mechanism detects if there is a loop device "
"associated with a file determined by the device and inode numbers – or if "
"creating a new loop device is necessary."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/system/template-implementation.rst:89
#: 46e4a9553e5a4657aea7073d7e02d9b6
msgid ""
"When an AppVM is stopped the xen hotplug script checks whether the device is "
"still in use – if it is not, the script removes the snapshot and frees the "
"loop device."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/system/template-implementation.rst:92
#: ada7faa854914bed951101e941fa7647
msgid "Changes to template filesystem"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/system/template-implementation.rst:95
#: 41a98ff16bce4f85b67d2d92e6726ce7
msgid ""
"In order for the full potential of the snapshot device to be realized, every "
"change in root.img must save the original version of the modified block in "
"root-cow.img. This is achieved by a snapshot-origin device."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/system/template-implementation.rst:97
#: d5ad9ac04dea49bba7474264a16673e5
msgid ""
"When TemplateVM is started, it receives the snapshot-origin device connected "
"as a root device (in read-write mode). Therefore, every change to this "
"device is immediately saved in root.img – but remains invisible to the "
"AppVM, which uses the snapshot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/system/template-implementation.rst:99
#: 168296a403fd4067ab9d4923bcb630d7
msgid ""
"When TemplateVM is stopped, the xen script moves root-cow.img to root-"
"cow.img.old and creates a new one (using the ``qvm-template-commit`` tool). "
"The snapshot device will remain untouched due to the loop device, which uses "
"an actual file on the disk (by inode, not by name). Linux kernel frees the "
"old root-cow.img files as soon as they are unused by all snapshot devices "
"(to be exact, loop devices). The new root-cow.img file will get a new inode "
"number, and so new AppVMs will get new snapshot devices (with different "
"names)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/system/template-implementation.rst:102
#: 6c80be209054411a8afb9030cd09a7fe
msgid "Rollback template changes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/system/template-implementation.rst:105
#: 8ba5580cd191463bba5b103519a726d7
msgid ""
"There is possibility to rollback last template changes. Using the automatic "
"snapshot that is normally saved every time the template is shutdown."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/system/template-implementation.rst:107
#: d7e0f36a21414a87ada1df71d658dab0
msgid ""
"Refer to volume backup and revert :doc:`documentation </user/advanced-topics/"
"volume-backup-revert>` for more information."
msgstr ""

